Patch 7924: a read-only view of the Matching2 room and a join target, for Discord Rich Presence and Join with the game's own online menus.

Why: the port shows the online state on the player's Discord profile (in a room, members, host or not, the other player's online name)
and lets a friend join from Discord. The game's own Online Battle menus create, search and join the rooms; the port must neither
read the emulation's private state nor change the game's room requests.

Now: ps3_np_matching2_room() returns whether a started context is outside a room (1) or in one (2), with the room id, member count,
slots, whether this game owns it and the first other member's online name; any thread, under the state lock only, nothing logged.
ps3_np_matching2_set_join_target(room) makes every SearchRoom answer list that one room only (when it also passes the title's own
filters), and ps3_np_matching2_join_target() says what became of it: pending, listed, joined, gone, full, not in this search, or the
join failed. 0 clears it. Without a target nothing changes.

